      "math_academy_id": "q-72691",
      "sequence_position": 3,
      "problem": "Chantelle did an experiment in her Chemistry class. She heated a liquid whose initial temperature was $-{5.3}^{∘}\\,\\text{C}.$ After several minutes, the temperature of the liquid increased by ${24.7}^{∘}\\,\\text{C}$, at which point she decided to end the experiment. What was the final temperature of the liquid?",
      "worked_solution": "To determine the final temperature of the liquid, we add the variation in temperature to the initial temperature of the liquid. This gives\n\n$$\n-{5.3}^{∘}\\,\\text{C}+{24.7}^{∘}\\,\\text{C}={19.4}^{∘}\\,\\text{C}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the temperature of the liquid at the end of the experiment was ${19.4}^{∘}\\,\\text{C}.$",
